    "title": "Urgent Appeal: Waco Police Ask for Public's Help to Find Missing Man with Dementia - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Piggie ,\n8 hours ago\nThe City of Waco is asking for the community’s assistance in the search for 73-year-old Bennie Deckard, who was last seen in the 1500 block of Clark Avenue. According to the KCENT / Waco Police, Mr. Deckard has dementia, which may explain why he possibly wandered off or became disoriented.\nDownload the KSSM Mobile App Now Police Seek Public’s Help Locating Missing Man with Dementia in Waco Area Canva Unfortunately, there is limited information available regarding what Mr. Deckard was wearing at the time he went missing. However, a photo of him has been shared by the Waco Police to help the public identify him . This image provides the most accurate reference for his appearance, and residents are encouraged to look closely in case they’ve seen him in their area. The community is urged to stay alert and report any possible sightings or information. If anyone knows the whereabouts of Mr. Bennie Deckard, they are asked to immediately contact the Waco Police Department at (254) 750-7500 or simply dial 911.\nWaco Police Search Underway: Missing Man with Dementia Needs to Be Found The goal is to ensure that Mr. Deckard is found and returned home safely. Time is of the essence in missing persons cases, especially involving individuals with cognitive impairments. Please share this information and stay vigilant — your attention could make all the difference in bringing Mr. Deckard home.\n8 Safest Cities in Texas Here are the 8 safest cities in Texas Gallery Credit: Piggie Google Maps Keller Texas Keller Texas has some of the nicest people in this town, and plenty of job opportunities. Google Maps Hutto Texas Hutto is a small city right outside of Austin Texas. The tight knit city is so friendly that store close for football games early to show support. Google Maps Flower Mound Texas Flower Mound Texas in my opinion, is one of the best places to raise a family. This area is very family friendly. Google Maps Colleyville Texas Colleyville is a community in Texas where everyone looks after on another. That's safety at it's best. Google Maps Friendswood Texas With a \"friend\" in the beginning of it's name, you know you have to be surrounded by friendly and safe people. Goggle Maps Trophy Club Texas Trophy Club Texas has the perfect name! It's a town that shows and take proud in being safe and friendly. Google Maps West University Place West University Place is known for it's law enforcement who take pride in keeping the city safe. Goggle Map Highland Village I have family who live in Highland Village Texas, it's so safe there that people can keep their door unlocked. Here Are The Top 5 Safest Places To Raise A Family In Central Texas These are the top 5 safest places in Central Texas to raise a family. Gallery Credit: Piggie Google Maps Hutto Texas Hutto Texas has a population of over 30,000 people and is part of the Austin- Round Rock Metro. Only a total of 230 crimes in this city all together. A lot is not happen in Hutto which is perfect for families. Google Maps LakeWays Texas LakeWays Texas has a population over 19,000 people with Lake Travis right next door a beautiful safe small town to raise your family. Google Maps Elgin, Texas I LOVE Elgin, Texas I have personally been there and it's the most friendliest town I have ever been to in Texas. Google Maps Leander Texas Leander is a growing city outside of Austin Texas that screams family first in that community. Leander is a family oriented city for sure. Pinterest Cedar Park Texas Cedar Park is a low crime city outside of Austin Texas. It's probably on of the most beautiful towns in Central Texas. This List Of Texas's Top 7 Foods Is Going To Start A Debate A look at the top foods Texans love to eat. From sweet to spicy, see if you agree with this list of the state's favorite dishes. Gallery Credit: Tommy Paradise, Townsquare Media, Canva, Texas Treats Canva BBQ Canva Chili Canva Cobbler Canva Frito Pie Canva Kolache Canva Pecan Pie Canva Tex-Mex",
